CCC@mn1401.med.msu.edu (Chris C. Conner) writes:

>How do you use the set NETHACKOPTIONS=" ... " in NetHack 3.0j?
>I'm using a Unix machine.  I finally figured out why I couldn't 
>save my files, but now I'm stuck with creating a random player
>when I start up from scratch.

>I tried 
>   set NETHACKOPTIONS="name:foo-W"
>in my .cshrc.  Is that right?

Try using 
	setenv NETHACKOPTIONS 'name:foo-W,nopickup'
in your .cshrc.

Don't bother with the nopickup if for some weird reason you like it.

